       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Your patient's weight, kidney function, and liver function don't change that limit. A dose this high raises the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI bleeding, and hyponatremia, and it has no proven added benefit.\n\nPlease check these before I enter anything:\n- **Typo or unit error:** Did you mean 40 mg, 50 mg, or 100 mg? Typical dosing starts at 25\u201350 mg daily and goes up to 200 mg.\n- **Intended dose:** If you meant a higher dose on purpose, confirm it with your resident or attending. If it's a deliberate off-label dose, it should be documented with the reasoning.\n- **Other medications:** Check for other serotonergic drugs, QT-prolonging drugs, anticoagulants, and NSAIDs.\n\nTell me the corrected dose, for example \"sertraline 50 mg PO once daily.\" I'll enter it right away. If your supervising physician does want 400 mg, tell me and I can enter it with a note recording that they approved it."
      }
